Subject: [PATCH] test(core,cli): ACP honors providers.json maxTokens as the
 output cap (red first)

Test-only commit for fork patch 0009. With providers.json bedrock settings
carrying `maxTokens` and no per-turn cap:

- core createAgentModelFromConfig keeps providerConfig.maxOutputTokens as the
  gateway request's maxTokens; a per-turn cap (maxTokensPerTurn) still wins,
  and a provider config for a different provider contributes nothing;
- wire test through ACP buildConfig, core createAgentModelFromConfig, the real
  Bedrock vendor and a stubbed fetch: the Converse request carries
  inferenceConfig.maxTokens 4321, and a Mantle chat request for
  aws-mantle/qwen.qwen3-coder-next carries max_tokens 2345;
- a whole ACP prompt turn on the local backend (AcpAgent.prompt through the
  real ClineCore, session runtime and Bedrock vendor, stubbed fetch) sends
  inferenceConfig.maxTokens 4321.

Rebased onto cli-v3.0.71 (test files taken from the rebased fork patch 0008, old number 0009).
